1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-3--3b-choosing-a-dialect","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-3/3b-choosing-a-dialect","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-3/3b-choosing-a-dialect","sourceHash":"e362ad4754ec99d491f467b6d59caad32addf64689bcf6b798f5bf3acbb8889b","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:48.943Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"3B — Choosing a Dialect","zh":"3B——选择方言"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"what-youre-doing","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What You're Doing","zh":"你正在做什么"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Up until now, you've been learning \"the language\" in a broad sense — absorbing vocabulary, grammar, and patterns from whatever content you enjoy. You may have naturally gravitated toward a specific regional variety without realizing it, or you may have been mixing several.","zh":"直到现在，你一直是在广义上学习“这门语言”——从自己喜欢的各种内容中吸收词汇、语法和语言模式。你可能在不知不觉中自然偏向了某个特定的地区变体，也可能一直混合接触多种变体。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Either way, now is the time to make a deliberate choice about which dialect and accent you want to focus on.","zh":"无论是哪种情况，现在都是有意识地决定自己想重点学习哪种方言和口音的时候了。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This matters more for some languages than others. Spanish, English, Arabic, and Chinese have <em>huge</em> regional variation. Japanese or Korean have less.","zh":"这一点对某些语言比对其他语言更重要。西班牙语、英语、阿拉伯语和中文存在<em>巨大的</em>地区差异。日语或韩语的地区差异则较小。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"But every language has at least some differences in vocabulary, pronunciation, and phrasing between regions, and narrowing your focus helps in two ways: it gives your ears a consistent target to train on, and it sets you up for more natural-sounding speech when you start speaking in Phase 4.","zh":"但每种语言在不同地区之间至少都会存在一些词汇、发音和表达方式上的差异。缩小重点范围有两个好处：它能为你的耳朵提供一致的训练目标，也能让你在第4阶段开始说话时，更容易说出听起来自然的语言。"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This sub-phase can be short — a few days to a couple of weeks. If you already know exactly which dialect you want, your main task is to research its specific features and make sure your immersion content matches.","zh":"这个子阶段可以很短——几天到几周。如果你已经明确知道想学哪种方言，主要任务就是研究它的具体特征，并确保沉浸内容与之匹配。"}},{"id":"whats-new","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What's New","zh":"有什么新内容"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Dialect research</strong> — Spend some time learning about the major dialects of your target language. What are the differences in vocabulary, pronunciation, and grammar? Which dialects are considered \"standard\"? Which ones match the kind of people you want to talk to or the content you enjoy?","zh":"<strong>方言研究</strong>——花些时间了解目标语言的主要方言。它们在词汇、发音和语法上有哪些差异？哪些方言被认为是“标准”方言？哪些方言符合你想交流的对象，或符合你喜欢的内容？"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Don't overthink this. You can always adjust later. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/dialects-and-accents\">Dialects and Accents</a>","zh":"不要想得太复杂。以后随时可以调整。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/dialects-and-accents\">方言与口音</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Sound Study (dialect-specific)</strong> — Revisit the sound system of the language, but now focus specifically on the features of your chosen dialect. How does this accent handle certain vowels or consonants? Are there sounds that are dropped or merged? Are there intonation patterns that are distinctive? Even a brief deep-dive here will sharpen your ears. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/sound-study\">Sound Study</a>","zh":"<strong>声音研究（针对方言）</strong>——重新了解这门语言的声音系统，但这次要特别关注所选方言的特征。这种口音如何处理某些元音或辅音？有没有声音会被省略或合并？是否存在独特的语调模式？即使只进行简短的深入研究，也能让你的耳朵更加敏锐。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/sound-study\">声音研究</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Filter your immersion.</strong> Start choosing content specifically from your target dialect. If you've been watching shows from multiple countries or regions, narrow your focus. This isn't about avoiding all other dialects forever — it's about giving your brain a consistent model to learn from during this critical phase.","zh":"<strong>筛选你的沉浸内容。</strong>开始专门选择来自目标方言的内容。如果你之前看过来自多个国家或地区的节目，现在就缩小范围。这并不是要你永远避开其他方言，而是要在这个关键阶段为大脑提供一个一致的学习模型。"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Consider a Language Parent:</strong> We pick up a massive amount of our language habits from parents, early caregivers and teachers. You can sort of mimic this in your target language by choosing a few native speakers (with lots of avalible audio) who you'd like to sound like. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/language-parent\">Language Parent</a>","zh":"<strong>考虑选择一位语言家长：</strong>我们的大量语言习惯都来自父母、幼年照护者和老师。你可以在目标语言中进行类似的模仿：选择几位你希望模仿其说话方式的母语者，最好是他们拥有大量可用的音频材料。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/language-parent\">语言家长</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Understand speech registers.</strong> Native speakers don't always talk the same way. There's a big difference between how someone speaks in a news broadcast, a scripted TV show, a casual vlog, and a conversation with friends. Start paying attention to these differences — scripted speech is slower and clearer, casual speech is faster and messier. You'll need to understand all of them eventually. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/casual-vs-scripted-vs-careful-speech\">Casual vs Scripted vs Careful Speech</a>","zh":"<strong>理解语体。</strong>母语者并不总是以同一种方式说话。新闻播报、电视剧台词、轻松的视频博客，以及和朋友聊天之间，存在很大差别。开始留意这些差异——台词通常更慢、更清晰，随意的日常表达则更快、更不规整。最终你需要理解所有这些语体。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/casual-vs-scripted-vs-careful-speech\">随意表达、台词与谨慎表达</a>"}},{"id":"your-routine","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Your Routine","zh":"你的日常安排"}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Priming drops as you shift focus to listening practice: <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">The Pillars of Language Learning</a>","zh":"随着重点转向听力练习，预热所占时间会减少：<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">语言学习的支柱</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Priming:</strong> 10%","zh":"<strong>预热：</strong>10%"},{"en":"<strong>Interactive Immersion:</strong> 50%","zh":"<strong>互动式沉浸：</strong>50%"},{"en":"<strong>Freeflow Immersion:</strong> 40%","zh":"<strong>自由流沉浸：</strong>40%"}]},{"id":"sample-daily-schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Sample Daily Schedule","zh":"每日安排示例"}},{"id":"segment-0018","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Dialect research and sound study: 10-20 mins","zh":"方言研究与声音研究：10—20分钟"},{"en":"Intensive Listening (content in chosen dialect): 50 mins","zh":"强化听力（所选方言的内容）：50分钟"},{"en":"Freeflow Listening (chosen dialect or language parent): 30 mins","zh":"自由流听力（所选方言或语言母语者）：30分钟"}]},{"id":"when-to-move-on","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Move On","zh":"何时进入下一阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0020","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Move to 3C when you:","zh":"满足以下条件后进入3C："}},{"id":"segment-0021","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Have chosen a target dialect and accent","zh":"已经选定目标方言和口音"},{"en":"Can identify most of the specific features of that dialect (pronunciation, vocabulary, phrasing)","zh":"能够识别该方言的大多数具体特征（发音、词汇、措辞）"},{"en":"Have shifted your immersion content to primarily feature that dialect","zh":"已经将沉浸内容调整为主要呈现该方言的内容"}]},{"id":"segment-0022","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<em>Stage 3B can be one of the shortest stages in the entier process, taking as little as a week or even a few days.</em>","zh":"<em>第三阶段B可能是整个过程中特别短的阶段之一，最短只需一周，甚至几天。</em>"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
